Title: Fix swarm-session aborting on unbound GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL
Linked issue: #12 ops/swarm-session fails: GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL unbound variable
Paths touched (1): ops/swarm-session
Body:
Computes the bot email once and assigns both variables from it, rather than reading `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL` in the same `export` that defines it.

**Tested end to end** with a stub `claude` on PATH. `ops/swarm-session planner` now reaches launch with:
- the role's opener prompt;
- `gh` resolving to the shim, and an installation token that works;
- the author and committer set to `productswarm-planner[bot]` with its noreply email;
- no `GH_TOKEN` or `GITHUB_TOKEN` inherited from your shell;
- the App's credential helper in effect.

Closes #12

